1
00:03:19,666 --> 00:03:25,416
DELUSION

2
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:37,666
Where's Yod now?

3
00:03:38,458 --> 00:03:41,750
I'm supposed to go home now.
And he told me I could go home now.

4
00:03:41,833 --> 00:03:42,916
You can go home soon.

5
00:03:44,083 --> 00:03:45,708
I need your help here, Uncle.

6
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Hmph.

7
00:03:54,708 --> 00:03:56,916
You worked at headquarters, yeah?

8
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:57,833
Mmm.

9
00:03:58,875 --> 00:04:00,916
Commendations in a senior position, too.

10
00:04:01,541 --> 00:04:02,375
Yeah.

11
00:04:03,916 --> 00:04:04,875
Uh…

12
00:04:06,916 --> 00:04:07,750
Now, Uncle,

13
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:11,583
what can you tell me about this ghost?

14
00:04:14,041 --> 00:04:15,000
What happened?

15
00:04:17,083 --> 00:04:17,916
Hey,

16
00:04:18,625 --> 00:04:20,166
who got taken this time, huh?

17
00:04:24,083 --> 00:04:27,083
A boy named Mued. Grandson of Paew.

18
00:04:30,041 --> 00:04:31,250
Grandson of Paew?

19
00:04:34,083 --> 00:04:35,666
Hey, Paew doesn't have a grandson.

20
00:04:37,125 --> 00:04:38,375
Her son isn't even married.

21
00:04:40,708 --> 00:04:42,208
Ah, that's okay, Uncle.

22
00:04:43,041 --> 00:04:43,875
It doesn't matter.

23
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:45,833
In any case,

24
00:04:46,791 --> 00:04:47,958
would you be able to help me?

25
00:04:49,416 --> 00:04:50,541
Who is Phii Pong?

26
00:04:53,333 --> 00:04:54,166
Look,

27
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:56,833
people believe that the spirit

28
00:04:57,458 --> 00:04:59,125
only possesses adults.

29
00:05:00,166 --> 00:05:01,833
The truth is, it's in children.

30
00:05:04,958 --> 00:05:05,916
Kids?

31
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:06,833
Yeah.

32
00:05:09,375 --> 00:05:10,458
You mean your grandson?

33
00:05:13,458 --> 00:05:14,291
Grandson?

34
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:15,875
Who's that?

35
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,041
Oh. The son of your daughter

36
00:05:20,958 --> 00:05:22,375
who came into the forest.

37
00:05:24,541 --> 00:05:25,833
Is Aim Phii Pong, Uncle?

38
00:05:27,041 --> 00:05:28,875
I don't know that.

39
00:05:29,708 --> 00:05:31,625
All I know is he's a kid,

40
00:05:31,708 --> 00:05:33,500
but I don't know whose child he is.

41
00:05:35,875 --> 00:05:38,333
So, we're done here, right?
I'm going home now.

42
00:05:38,416 --> 00:05:41,208
Not yet, Uncle. I've just got
a few more questions for you.

43
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,083
Let me out of here!
What am I locked up for, anyway?

44
00:05:45,208 --> 00:05:46,833
I'm a civil servant, dammit!

45
00:05:47,958 --> 00:05:49,375
- Calm down.
- Let me go!

46
00:05:49,458 --> 00:05:50,416
- Let me go!
- Come on!

47
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:52,375
Uncle, calm down. I'm just trying to talk.

48
00:05:52,458 --> 00:05:55,000
I don't give a damn who you think you are!
I'm not afraid of you

49
00:05:55,083 --> 00:05:57,583
because I didn't do any of it! Let me go!

50
00:05:58,083 --> 00:06:00,500
Sergeant, can we get a DNA sample?

51
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,375
Nee!

52
00:06:03,541 --> 00:06:04,583
Nee!

53
00:06:04,666 --> 00:06:06,750
Come and talk to these people for me.

54
00:06:06,833 --> 00:06:08,750
Nee! Come here!

55
00:06:08,833 --> 00:06:11,583
CHIANG KHAN HOSPITAL

56
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:17,250
How could you let that happen
to our child?

57
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:20,458
The police told me everything.

58
00:06:23,916 --> 00:06:25,500
You're lucky I'm not pressing charges.

59
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:28,000
Charges for what?

60
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:31,500
For playing with his own grandson?

61
00:06:43,750 --> 00:06:45,000
I'm taking him home right now.

62
00:06:48,166 --> 00:06:51,250
And you'll dump him at your mom's
while you go somewhere else.

63
00:06:52,458 --> 00:06:54,166
Why shouldn't he stay with me?

64
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,166
Hasn't he told you?

65
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:58,166
He doesn't want to go to Grandma's.

66
00:07:02,041 --> 00:07:05,083
Better than a house
with a crazy bastard walking around.

67
00:07:12,875 --> 00:07:13,875
Even if you leave,

68
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,958
he'll stay with me, anyway.

69
00:07:18,791 --> 00:07:20,125
Your family is so poor.

70
00:07:20,875 --> 00:07:22,500
How could you give him a good life?

71
00:07:23,250 --> 00:07:25,125
You can't even keep him fucking safe.

72
00:07:27,416 --> 00:07:28,250
Poor, sure.

73
00:07:30,041 --> 00:07:32,458
But I didn't leave him
to go out and fuck around.

74
00:07:34,833 --> 00:07:36,333
I'm only seeing one person.

75
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:40,375
And I'm happy.

76
00:07:42,125 --> 00:07:43,541
So stop talking nonsense.

77
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,708
People will get the wrong idea
and think she's my mistress.

78
00:07:50,375 --> 00:07:52,041
Just agree to the divorce.

79
00:07:56,458 --> 00:07:57,333
Everyone…

80
00:07:59,291 --> 00:08:01,000
can tell we don't love each other.

81
00:08:09,875 --> 00:08:10,750
Pa!

82
00:08:11,666 --> 00:08:13,375
- Aim. Oh!
- I'm okay. See?

83
00:08:13,458 --> 00:08:14,958
Oh, my son!

84
00:08:16,625 --> 00:08:18,666
You all right, little boy? Oh.

85
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:23,500
Listen, you're staying
at my house tonight. Okay?

86
00:08:23,583 --> 00:08:27,708
Oh! You know, you had me worried sick.
Let me look at you. Oh.

87
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:31,291
Oh, okay. Okay, you're okay. You're okay.

88
00:08:32,875 --> 00:08:35,500
2014 MURDER CASES
CASES 1-10

89
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:43,583
Uh, Inspector?

90
00:08:50,333 --> 00:08:52,708
"Phii Pong Murders."
Are these all the files from the time?

91
00:08:53,541 --> 00:08:55,666
Yes, Inspector. This is all we have.

92
00:08:56,458 --> 00:08:58,166
We don't get many big cases around here.

93
00:09:08,625 --> 00:09:09,583
MURDER CASE FILE

94
00:09:11,041 --> 00:09:13,125
Ah, that one. That's the Phii Pong case

95
00:09:13,208 --> 00:09:14,375
from more than ten years ago.

96
00:09:30,458 --> 00:09:34,083
THONGDEE SUMPLOY - COMPLAINANT
POL. LT. SOMSAK PATHAM - RECORDING OFFICER

97
00:09:42,541 --> 00:09:45,000
Be careful not to scratch it too much,
or it'll scar.

98
00:09:47,166 --> 00:09:48,250
But it itches, Mom.

99
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:52,416
Does it hurt?

100
00:09:54,208 --> 00:09:55,708
Um, only a little.

101
00:09:56,583 --> 00:09:59,458
You know when soccer running hurt my chin?
That was worse.

102
00:10:00,458 --> 00:10:01,666
Hmm. Let's see.

103
00:10:03,958 --> 00:10:04,833
Oh.

104
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:07,291
- The doctor did a good job.
- Ooh.

105
00:10:11,750 --> 00:10:12,875
- Aim.
- Hmm?

106
00:10:14,916 --> 00:10:15,791
Sorry.

107
00:10:18,875 --> 00:10:20,041
What are you sorry for?

108
00:10:22,541 --> 00:10:23,708
You don't have to be sorry.

109
00:10:28,458 --> 00:10:30,833
Aim, why did you follow Grandpa
into the woods?

110
00:10:31,416 --> 00:10:32,291
Hmm?

111
00:10:34,416 --> 00:10:38,333
I wanted to know if Phii Pong was Grandpa.

112
00:10:40,875 --> 00:10:42,125
Grandpa is just unwell.

113
00:10:42,916 --> 00:10:44,208
You and I know that.

114
00:10:45,583 --> 00:10:47,916
Um, I wanted to get some proof.

115
00:10:48,916 --> 00:10:51,500
Because everyone was saying things,

116
00:10:51,583 --> 00:10:53,500
and I wanted to know the truth.

117
00:10:56,125 --> 00:10:57,041
Hmm.

118
00:10:58,041 --> 00:11:01,458
But did Grandpa scare you?

119
00:11:04,416 --> 00:11:06,041
How did you end up in the water?

120
00:11:13,583 --> 00:11:14,833
You can go back with Dad.

121
00:11:14,916 --> 00:11:18,375
I have to stay and look after Grandpa,
but I'll be back soon, okay?

122
00:11:18,458 --> 00:11:19,791
- Mmm-hmm.
- Come on.

123
00:11:27,416 --> 00:11:28,458
Hold on a second, Wat.

124
00:11:29,166 --> 00:11:30,125
- Aim?
- Mmm?

125
00:11:32,958 --> 00:11:34,041
Did you forget something?

126
00:11:35,791 --> 00:11:37,125
Pew.

127
00:11:37,708 --> 00:11:39,041
- Bye-bye.
- See you soon.

128
00:11:39,875 --> 00:11:40,916
I'll call you, okay?

129
00:11:41,875 --> 00:11:42,708
Come on.

130
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:02,875
All these murder cases,
you're the only one still around?

131
00:12:03,583 --> 00:12:04,416
Yep.

132
00:12:05,375 --> 00:12:07,750
Because then, there were only a few of us.

133
00:12:07,833 --> 00:12:09,916
Now they're all either dead or retired.

134
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,375
So what do you think, Sergeant?

135
00:12:12,458 --> 00:12:13,416
Think?

136
00:12:16,125 --> 00:12:17,625
Is it a ghost or a person?

137
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,708
I may be small-town,
but I'm not an idiot, Inspector.

138
00:12:24,625 --> 00:12:27,125
But back then, we couldn't talk to anyone.

139
00:12:28,750 --> 00:12:31,291
It did cross my mind
it could be a ghost.

140
00:12:32,041 --> 00:12:35,833
City guy like you probably hears that
and thinks we're ridiculous, right?

141
00:13:05,875 --> 00:13:08,750
<i>Sis, they're keeping Dad in custody.</i>

142
00:13:10,333 --> 00:13:11,250
What the… What?

143
00:13:12,416 --> 00:13:13,333
Can they do that?

144
00:13:14,375 --> 00:13:17,875
<i>Well, I think it might be better</i>
<i>if Dad stays here for a while.</i>

145
00:13:18,666 --> 00:13:21,958
Because if something happens
while he is here,

146
00:13:22,041 --> 00:13:23,875
maybe they will stop saying
he is possessed.

147
00:13:24,875 --> 00:13:26,083
What about Ma?

148
00:13:26,666 --> 00:13:27,708
She's here with me.

149
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:31,458
I'm about to take her home.
See you at the house.

150
00:14:03,041 --> 00:14:04,666
So, he moved here, yeah?

151
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:05,750
That's right, Inspector.

152
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:15,666
Hey there.

153
00:14:19,250 --> 00:14:20,125
Sir, a few questions.

154
00:14:20,208 --> 00:14:21,541
Can I help?

155
00:14:21,625 --> 00:14:23,291
This is our new inspector.

156
00:14:23,375 --> 00:14:24,375
Hello, sir.

157
00:14:25,125 --> 00:14:26,708
I'm here to ask about your son.

158
00:14:30,875 --> 00:14:32,791
I didn't think much of it.

159
00:14:32,875 --> 00:14:36,208
Around here, it's normal for kids
to be playing out in the fields.

160
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:39,041
If I'd known there was an evil ghost,

161
00:14:39,833 --> 00:14:41,625
I never would have let him go.

162
00:14:42,791 --> 00:14:43,833
Thinking carefully,

163
00:14:44,583 --> 00:14:47,458
did anyone from outside the village
move in at that time?

164
00:14:50,416 --> 00:14:52,083
That I remember, no, Officer.

165
00:14:53,625 --> 00:14:56,583
Aside from Phii Pong,
is there anyone else you suspected?

166
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:18,166
There was no ghost.

167
00:15:19,875 --> 00:15:21,625
Do ghosts hunt and kill kids?

168
00:15:23,541 --> 00:15:24,750
The cops were just lazy.

169
00:15:24,833 --> 00:15:27,750
They repeat what others say
so they don't have to do their jobs.

170
00:15:27,833 --> 00:15:29,000
Hey, Bua.

171
00:15:29,083 --> 00:15:32,000
Your son wasn't killed by a ghost.

172
00:15:32,083 --> 00:15:34,125
No? Well, who do you think did it then?

173
00:15:34,208 --> 00:15:36,250
I don't know. That your job, isn't it?

174
00:15:38,083 --> 00:15:40,333
And who brought up Phii Pong
for the first time?

175
00:15:41,625 --> 00:15:45,291
If it wasn't the cops,
it was the shaman around here.

176
00:15:45,375 --> 00:15:47,833
Just repeating the same thing for years

177
00:15:47,916 --> 00:15:51,416
while nobody bothered to look
for the person who killed my son.

178
00:15:58,583 --> 00:15:59,708
I'm sorry, officers.

179
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:27,375
Just heat up the leftovers and eat that.
The day is wasted.

180
00:16:27,458 --> 00:16:29,333
There's no time for anything now.

181
00:16:29,416 --> 00:16:33,291
Okay, I will. Do you take
your medicine before you eat?

182
00:16:33,375 --> 00:16:35,416
Are you doing anything later this evening?

183
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:38,125
Take me up, up to the police station.

184
00:16:39,666 --> 00:16:41,000
Your father's on his own.

185
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:43,666
He's not in his right mind.
We can't leave him there.

186
00:16:47,250 --> 00:16:48,333
I'll go on my own.

187
00:16:49,458 --> 00:16:51,666
Now just look at the mess we're in.

188
00:16:51,750 --> 00:16:55,250
It would have been all right,
but you had to go and call the police.

189
00:16:55,333 --> 00:16:56,958
And now they've locked him up.

190
00:16:57,791 --> 00:16:59,541
The whole town is gossiping.

191
00:17:01,166 --> 00:17:02,750
Here, put this in the fridge for me.

192
00:17:07,833 --> 00:17:08,666
Wan.

193
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:10,833
Can you please lend me some cash?

194
00:17:13,250 --> 00:17:14,125
I don't have any.

195
00:17:15,708 --> 00:17:18,541
You don't have any? What do you mean?
Your husband is rich.

196
00:17:18,625 --> 00:17:20,208
His family is rich as hell.

197
00:17:20,916 --> 00:17:23,375
And what about you?
Don't you have any savings of your own?

198
00:17:25,208 --> 00:17:28,875
My savings? I send you money all the time,
don't you remember?

199
00:17:30,291 --> 00:17:31,666
Are you getting dementia as well?

200
00:17:35,666 --> 00:17:36,666
Take your medicine.

201
00:17:57,791 --> 00:17:59,000
Here, sis, let me help.

202
00:18:00,625 --> 00:18:01,750
Come on. Let me help.

203
00:18:03,875 --> 00:18:06,458
Is this enough? If not,
I can make an omelette.

204
00:18:06,541 --> 00:18:08,083
Plenty, sis. It's great.

205
00:18:09,833 --> 00:18:12,083
Hardly, when her son is eating, too.

206
00:18:21,625 --> 00:18:23,208
Hey, do we have any chilly?

207
00:18:23,875 --> 00:18:26,458
Add lots of chilly, okay?
Make it really spicy.

208
00:18:26,541 --> 00:18:28,708
The way we used to eat it
when we were kids, remember?

209
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:47,541
Oh, and, um, Dad's hospital bills,

210
00:18:48,625 --> 00:18:49,875
I can sort it out.

211
00:18:51,625 --> 00:18:54,166
And about Mom wanting to borrow money,

212
00:18:55,375 --> 00:18:56,375
I'll give it to you.

213
00:18:58,125 --> 00:18:59,583
You transfer it to her.

214
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:02,166
Why don't you just give her the money,

215
00:19:03,583 --> 00:19:04,833
and leave me out of it?

216
00:19:08,125 --> 00:19:11,416
If you're lending her money,
don't start with it all.

217
00:19:12,208 --> 00:19:13,083
Hold some back.

218
00:19:14,375 --> 00:19:16,666
Just in case we have to put Dad
into permanent care.

219
00:19:16,750 --> 00:19:17,958
Mm.

220
00:19:22,083 --> 00:19:25,583
Poor Aim falling in the water.
Did he end up saying who did it?

221
00:19:27,250 --> 00:19:29,666
Um, it wasn't Dad, was it?

222
00:19:31,458 --> 00:19:33,208
Aim really loves his grandpa.

223
00:19:34,708 --> 00:19:37,458
He just slipped.
Dad tried to help him, but he couldn't.

224
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,125
Oh.

225
00:19:41,541 --> 00:19:42,541
Hmm.

226
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,541
Regarding the cause of death,

227
00:19:54,625 --> 00:19:57,500
it was a severe blunt force trauma
to the head.

228
00:19:58,166 --> 00:20:00,375
We found absolutely no defensive wounds.

229
00:20:00,458 --> 00:20:04,333
So it's very probable
that one blow caused death.

230
00:20:05,041 --> 00:20:07,500
Or at the very least,
immediate loss of consciousness.

231
00:20:12,166 --> 00:20:14,000
Sergeant, you can step out if you need to.

232
00:20:14,083 --> 00:20:15,208
Yeah, I'll be outside.

233
00:20:17,166 --> 00:20:18,791
What about the wound on his abdomen?

234
00:20:23,666 --> 00:20:26,208
Well, this injury is postmortem.

235
00:20:26,291 --> 00:20:29,375
So it happened just after
the victim has been killed.

236
00:20:30,666 --> 00:20:33,250
Is it possible to determine
what weapon was used?

237
00:20:35,458 --> 00:20:36,791
It's hard to say, Inspector.

238
00:20:36,875 --> 00:20:40,291
All we know is that
it was a sharp, hard object.

239
00:20:40,375 --> 00:20:44,583
If you find any potential weapons,
uh, around the crime scene,

240
00:20:44,666 --> 00:20:45,791
we can compare them.

241
00:20:47,625 --> 00:20:48,458
Okay.

242
00:20:49,208 --> 00:20:51,625
Oh, yes, and he tested positive
for amphetamines.

243
00:21:01,708 --> 00:21:04,416
WOUND ASSESSMENT FORM
ANUPONG NALAH

244
00:21:18,333 --> 00:21:19,625
Do you think it's possible

245
00:21:19,708 --> 00:21:21,666
the perpetrator is the same
for these cases?

246
00:21:26,875 --> 00:21:29,875
This is another case
from more than ten years ago.

247
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:33,833
The victim's teeth were also taken out.

248
00:21:37,291 --> 00:21:40,583
Both cases show
very similar patterns of death,

249
00:21:40,666 --> 00:21:42,458
especially with the missing teeth.

250
00:21:44,583 --> 00:21:48,083
I'd be surprised if there's not
more evidence at the crime scene.

251
00:21:48,166 --> 00:21:49,833
I'm sure you'll find some answers there.

252
00:22:00,875 --> 00:22:01,833
Sergeant.

253
00:22:02,708 --> 00:22:04,583
- Hmm.
- We need to follow up on the evidence.

254
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,750
Um, I'm gonna get going, sir.

255
00:22:16,125 --> 00:22:17,333
There you go.

256
00:22:25,291 --> 00:22:26,291
People are scared.

257
00:22:27,500 --> 00:22:28,916
He's in custody for now.

258
00:22:31,166 --> 00:22:32,833
He's not a suspect, I'm assuming.

259
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:40,833
You know,

260
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:45,166
the closest person to the scene
was your dad.

261
00:22:45,250 --> 00:22:47,166
And we found a grey hair on the body,

262
00:22:47,958 --> 00:22:49,208
so he's a person of interest.

263
00:22:49,958 --> 00:22:53,375
We've sent it for DNA testing.
If it doesn't match, there's no issue.

264
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:59,666
You can't be saying
someone in my dad's condition

265
00:23:02,375 --> 00:23:03,666
is capable of this.

266
00:23:05,666 --> 00:23:07,083
I mean, it's hilarious

267
00:23:08,208 --> 00:23:11,083
that people still believe
in this Phii Pong craziness.

268
00:23:12,958 --> 00:23:14,666
Back then, how do you remember it?

269
00:23:17,083 --> 00:23:18,000
I don't.

270
00:23:20,208 --> 00:23:21,583
Someone died near your home.

271
00:23:22,166 --> 00:23:23,500
Weren't you a little scared?

272
00:23:25,541 --> 00:23:26,458
No way.

273
00:23:27,375 --> 00:23:28,625
Not about it being a ghost.

274
00:23:30,083 --> 00:23:34,166
And so were there any rumors or gossip
about the identity of Phii Pong?

275
00:23:36,083 --> 00:23:37,166
No, there wasn't.

276
00:23:40,458 --> 00:23:42,875
I remember people started hanging
those scarecrows.

277
00:23:44,666 --> 00:23:46,916
You've got a younger brother, right?
Did he hang one?

278
00:23:51,791 --> 00:23:52,750
No, he didn't.

279
00:23:54,208 --> 00:23:55,208
Ma put one up.

280
00:23:56,458 --> 00:23:59,708
Although my dad didn't really believe
in it. He just let her hang it.

281
00:24:02,041 --> 00:24:05,000
But not long after,
he sent my brother to study in Bangkok.

282
00:24:12,125 --> 00:24:14,416
MURDER CASE FILE

283
00:24:17,666 --> 00:24:20,500
You're from the city,
but you believe in ghosts?

284
00:24:26,041 --> 00:24:27,875
You seem so fascinated by it.

285
00:24:28,958 --> 00:24:31,500
I think you're starting to believe
that my dad's a ghost.

286
00:24:35,333 --> 00:24:36,666
If not, that's good.

287
00:24:40,166 --> 00:24:43,958
Justice will prevail, and I know
my dad will be treated properly.

288
00:24:52,166 --> 00:24:53,500
Open up!

289
00:24:53,583 --> 00:24:57,416
- Ugh, what is it now, old man?
- Open the door! Open it!

290
00:24:58,041 --> 00:24:59,125
Open it!

291
00:24:59,208 --> 00:25:00,083
Dad!

292
00:25:01,291 --> 00:25:03,666
Dad, wait a second. I'll ask the officer.

293
00:25:04,250 --> 00:25:05,916
Tell me why I'm locked up in here.

294
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,041
But you're not.

295
00:25:10,583 --> 00:25:12,125
You're helping them investigate.

296
00:25:12,875 --> 00:25:15,708
But it is a secret,
so the door has to be locked.

297
00:25:20,833 --> 00:25:22,250
What do you need, Dad?

298
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:25,208
I need the bathroom.

299
00:25:26,708 --> 00:25:28,208
Open up.

300
00:25:29,250 --> 00:25:30,083
It's okay.

301
00:25:36,833 --> 00:25:40,375
Dad, just go with the officer, okay?
I'll be here, all right?

302
00:25:41,125 --> 00:25:42,375
Yeah.

303
00:25:50,625 --> 00:25:53,291
If you can keep your dad
from going anywhere,

304
00:25:54,291 --> 00:25:55,791
then maybe we can release him.

305
00:25:59,041 --> 00:26:00,083
So you can rest up.

306
00:26:48,666 --> 00:26:51,000
Won't it hurt him, tying him up like this?

307
00:26:54,416 --> 00:26:57,125
Well, just how it has to be for now.

308
00:26:58,041 --> 00:27:01,541
But I'll find something that works better
at the psych ward.

309
00:27:03,083 --> 00:27:06,083
Also, I've adjusted his medication.

310
00:27:06,166 --> 00:27:08,333
If he stops having these mood swings,

311
00:27:09,125 --> 00:27:10,625
we won't have to tie him down.

312
00:27:17,375 --> 00:27:18,458
I can watch over him.

313
00:27:19,791 --> 00:27:21,750
Sis, get some sleep.

314
00:27:41,750 --> 00:27:44,666
- I put in my share.
- 100 baht each. I've given.

315
00:27:46,083 --> 00:27:48,166
- Who said that?
- I remember now.

316
00:27:48,250 --> 00:27:49,583
That's what happened.

317
00:27:49,666 --> 00:27:51,958
You went to the cremation, right?

318
00:27:52,041 --> 00:27:53,958
- You went, didn't you?
- I did.

319
00:27:54,041 --> 00:27:55,291
- Did you go?
- I did.

320
00:27:56,125 --> 00:27:58,125
It was very sad.

321
00:28:08,541 --> 00:28:09,916
I'm sorry for your loss.

322
00:28:27,916 --> 00:28:30,708
BORN 9 SEPTEMBER 2011
DIED 31 OCTOBER 2026

323
00:28:32,083 --> 00:28:33,125
What are you making?

324
00:28:34,041 --> 00:28:35,041
Fish congee.

325
00:28:37,416 --> 00:28:39,208
Here, let me help you.

326
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:49,000
Ey, Nee.

327
00:28:50,416 --> 00:28:51,416
Where's your husband?

328
00:28:55,833 --> 00:28:56,666
At home.

329
00:28:57,708 --> 00:28:59,708
- Wat is helping to look after him.
- Huh?

330
00:29:00,583 --> 00:29:02,458
The police let him out already?

331
00:29:03,833 --> 00:29:04,833
Mmm.

332
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:07,750
And what if he runs off again, Nee?

333
00:29:10,833 --> 00:29:13,083
Why didn't you leave him
with the police for a while?

334
00:29:14,041 --> 00:29:17,250
Stupid to let him out.
What if the Phii Pong possesses him again?

335
00:29:20,166 --> 00:29:21,416
Hello, Shaman Sak.

336
00:29:21,500 --> 00:29:22,541
Hello.

337
00:29:25,541 --> 00:29:26,708
My condolences.

338
00:29:45,083 --> 00:29:47,083
Human teeth are really tiny.

339
00:29:48,375 --> 00:29:49,291
Hard to find.

340
00:29:50,291 --> 00:29:52,875
Hmm. How many are missing again?

341
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:55,958
Mmm, how many?

342
00:29:57,458 --> 00:29:58,291
Five.

343
00:29:58,833 --> 00:30:01,916
Two incisors, one canine,
and two molars.

344
00:30:07,333 --> 00:30:08,166
Ready?

345
00:30:09,333 --> 00:30:10,625
The drone is ready, Inspector.

346
00:30:24,833 --> 00:30:26,083
The boy went in pretty deep.

347
00:30:38,750 --> 00:30:39,583
Hold up.

348
00:30:41,500 --> 00:30:42,708
What's that?

349
00:31:01,750 --> 00:31:03,041
- Sergeant.
- Yes, sir?

350
00:31:03,541 --> 00:31:05,333
Back then, who knew
this house was here?

351
00:31:06,250 --> 00:31:09,083
In the old days, you couldn't
get this deep in the forest, sir.

352
00:31:10,958 --> 00:31:13,875
So nobody knew that it was here,
or who built it?

353
00:33:16,666 --> 00:33:18,958
<i>And today we're going to prove it,</i>

354
00:33:19,750 --> 00:33:22,458
<i>the story of Phii Pong here in Nasao.</i>

355
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:24,875
<i>- What's the truth behind it…</i>
- Nee!

356
00:33:25,916 --> 00:33:27,000
Nee, are you home?

357
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:29,833
Nee!

358
00:33:31,416 --> 00:33:32,583
Nee, are you there?

359
00:33:32,666 --> 00:33:33,500
Who is it?

360
00:33:34,250 --> 00:33:35,250
How should I know?

361
00:33:51,875 --> 00:33:53,291
What are you doing here?

362
00:33:54,291 --> 00:33:57,791
Let Sak do a ritual.
It's no big deal. You're better off safe.

363
00:33:59,416 --> 00:34:02,416
Come on now, we're all family.
This isn't so hard.

364
00:34:04,916 --> 00:34:07,250
Now I'll just go in and speak
to Narong for a while.

365
00:34:09,833 --> 00:34:12,416
Please come back. He's asleep now.

366
00:34:15,208 --> 00:34:17,041
Are you two alone in there?

367
00:34:18,875 --> 00:34:20,083
How about Wat?

368
00:34:20,166 --> 00:34:21,375
Wat's at work.

369
00:34:22,291 --> 00:34:23,208
Come on, go.

370
00:34:23,291 --> 00:34:24,750
You're going to wake Narong up.

371
00:34:28,166 --> 00:34:29,000
Who is it?

372
00:34:32,500 --> 00:34:34,166
Let me go!

373
00:34:34,250 --> 00:34:35,333
Let me go!

374
00:34:36,166 --> 00:34:37,125
Let me go!

375
00:34:37,208 --> 00:34:41,958
- Sadhu, sadhu, sadhu.
- Stupid snake oil idiot.

376
00:34:42,041 --> 00:34:44,291
Truly, the Blessed One is worthy.

377
00:34:44,375 --> 00:34:48,166
Homage to the body of Buddha.
Bind it. Bind it.

378
00:34:50,041 --> 00:34:51,791
I said, let me go!

379
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:59,000
Uh, Inspector, we found some more teeth.

380
00:35:07,791 --> 00:35:09,000
The spot we found Mued,

381
00:35:10,083 --> 00:35:12,041
and the place
where the mechanic's kid was found

382
00:35:12,625 --> 00:35:13,625
are both near the hut.

383
00:35:27,625 --> 00:35:28,458
Guts.

384
00:35:29,208 --> 00:35:30,083
Teeth.

385
00:35:30,166 --> 00:35:31,625
Blunt force to the head.

386
00:35:33,250 --> 00:35:34,083
Phii Pong.

387
00:35:39,083 --> 00:35:41,791
Sergeant, maybe we pay
that shaman a visit.

388
00:36:01,291 --> 00:36:02,791
Wanna skip taekwondo today,

389
00:36:04,208 --> 00:36:05,166
and eat shabu?

390
00:36:07,291 --> 00:36:08,708
Can we do it later, Mom?

391
00:36:09,666 --> 00:36:12,458
I've got my red belt exam. I wanna pass.

392
00:36:14,916 --> 00:36:17,291
Are you sure you're ready for it?

393
00:36:17,375 --> 00:36:18,375
It's in the bag.

394
00:36:24,500 --> 00:36:26,125
Wanna come see Grandma and Grandpa?

395
00:36:27,625 --> 00:36:28,458
How about that?

396
00:36:32,375 --> 00:36:34,791
I have to work tomorrow,
so we can come back together.

397
00:36:42,375 --> 00:36:43,208
Okay.

398
00:36:43,958 --> 00:36:44,916
Will Dad mind?

399
00:36:50,083 --> 00:36:51,708
Never mind. Go with Dad.

400
00:36:53,125 --> 00:36:55,708
If you came with me, we'd have
to wake up early, anyway.

401
00:36:55,791 --> 00:36:57,291
I'll see you tomorrow though.

402
00:37:10,666 --> 00:37:11,708
Hello, Grandma.

403
00:37:13,458 --> 00:37:15,250
Oh, I see your car.

404
00:37:16,666 --> 00:37:17,750
I'm coming out now.

405
00:37:23,583 --> 00:37:27,333
Here. Dad's old phone is mine now.

406
00:37:44,625 --> 00:37:47,375
Chew that properly, dear, or you'll choke.

407
00:37:47,458 --> 00:37:50,291
You're eating like that before class?
Won't you feel sick?

408
00:37:51,083 --> 00:37:52,416
Mmm-mmm.

409
00:37:54,041 --> 00:37:56,000
Mom, see you soon.

410
00:37:56,750 --> 00:37:58,208
Mmm-hmm. Ooh.

411
00:37:58,291 --> 00:37:59,250
Pssh.

412
00:38:08,500 --> 00:38:09,333
Hello.

413
00:38:12,125 --> 00:38:13,666
Is Yote with you?

414
00:38:14,916 --> 00:38:16,000
Yote's a busy man.

415
00:38:18,875 --> 00:38:19,833
What's he up to?

416
00:38:23,125 --> 00:38:24,625
He told me he'd pick up Aim.

417
00:38:25,833 --> 00:38:29,000
If he's too busy to come for his son,
he should have let me know.

418
00:38:30,416 --> 00:38:31,458
I'm here now.

419
00:38:33,458 --> 00:38:35,583
Yote had something come up suddenly.

420
00:38:36,708 --> 00:38:38,041
Oh, but you don't need to worry.

421
00:38:39,166 --> 00:38:41,500
Because I will keep
my grandson safe from harm.

422
00:38:44,833 --> 00:38:45,791
Bye-bye now.

423
00:38:45,875 --> 00:38:47,416
Don't want Aim to be late.

424
00:39:38,416 --> 00:39:40,125
What the hell?

425
00:39:56,583 --> 00:39:58,541
- Yote?
- Don't come out. There's glass here.

426
00:40:12,083 --> 00:40:12,916
YOTE

427
00:40:20,666 --> 00:40:22,208
YOTE

428
00:40:26,041 --> 00:40:26,958
YOTE

429
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:42,666
YOTE

430
00:40:46,375 --> 00:40:49,541
<i>Wan, I never thought</i>
<i>you could sink this low.</i>

431
00:40:49,625 --> 00:40:51,166
Now let me tell you something

432
00:40:51,875 --> 00:40:54,125
Doesn't matter what you say,
doesn't matter what you do,

433
00:40:54,208 --> 00:40:57,791
because you could hold a gun to my head,
and you'll get nothing from me!

434
00:41:08,583 --> 00:41:09,666
Between you and me,

435
00:41:10,875 --> 00:41:12,333
there is nothing left.

436
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:15,791
<i>I never considered playing dirty.</i>

437
00:41:17,166 --> 00:41:20,041
<i>But if that's way</i>
<i>you want to play it, game on.</i>

438
00:41:23,125 --> 00:41:23,958
And you know,

439
00:41:24,958 --> 00:41:26,125
forget about your son.

440
00:41:27,875 --> 00:41:31,166
<i>You'll never see him again, or my money.</i>

441
00:41:52,125 --> 00:41:53,625
- He's here.
- Mm.

442
00:41:59,208 --> 00:42:01,791
- Hello, Uncle.
- Hello. What brings you here?

443
00:42:03,250 --> 00:42:04,625
Have you been drinking?

444
00:42:07,500 --> 00:42:08,958
I only just arrived here,

445
00:42:09,458 --> 00:42:11,666
so I had my colleague
bring me to see you.

446
00:42:13,583 --> 00:42:15,375
What name should I use, Sarge?

447
00:42:16,208 --> 00:42:17,333
Master or Shaman?

448
00:42:18,958 --> 00:42:20,791
Oh, we just usually call him--

449
00:42:20,875 --> 00:42:22,416
Just call me "Uncle."

450
00:42:22,500 --> 00:42:23,500
Uh…

451
00:42:24,416 --> 00:42:26,166
And what's your name, son?

452
00:42:26,250 --> 00:42:27,583
I'm Pete.

453
00:42:52,833 --> 00:42:54,541
How long have you been doing this, Uncle?

454
00:42:56,625 --> 00:42:58,708
Quite a while. More than ten years.

455
00:43:01,083 --> 00:43:02,541
Ever since Phii Pong

456
00:43:03,875 --> 00:43:05,875
killed the mechanic's boy, am I right?

457
00:43:07,916 --> 00:43:10,833
Well, I don't recall.

458
00:43:19,041 --> 00:43:20,416
You knew the kid named Mued.

459
00:43:22,625 --> 00:43:23,875
I'm working on that case.

460
00:43:24,708 --> 00:43:26,291
And everyone keeps saying,

461
00:43:28,041 --> 00:43:31,041
"It's just like back then,
the case of the mechanic's boy."

462
00:43:32,583 --> 00:43:33,791
I bet you got some stories.

463
00:43:40,375 --> 00:43:42,291
I don't really know anything, you see.

464
00:43:44,208 --> 00:43:47,583
These stories that the old folks
passed down,

465
00:43:48,375 --> 00:43:49,500
that's about it.

466
00:43:53,083 --> 00:43:55,500
It was already happening
before that kid died?

467
00:43:58,458 --> 00:43:59,791
Beware the angry spirit.

468
00:44:01,250 --> 00:44:04,166
Everyone around here knows about it.

469
00:44:06,500 --> 00:44:07,375
Is that right?

470
00:44:08,458 --> 00:44:09,333
Yeah.

471
00:44:09,416 --> 00:44:10,291
Mm.

472
00:44:12,333 --> 00:44:13,958
But you left out some details.

473
00:44:14,041 --> 00:44:17,750
You said Phii Pong only eats human organs.

474
00:44:19,416 --> 00:44:21,083
But the bodies we found

475
00:44:22,041 --> 00:44:23,583
were missing other things.

476
00:44:30,666 --> 00:44:31,666
Hmm?

477
00:44:33,750 --> 00:44:38,083
A spirit will eat anything
that's on the table.

478
00:44:38,166 --> 00:44:39,916
It only needs to be careful

479
00:44:40,416 --> 00:44:42,291
not to let anyone who has seen it

480
00:44:43,125 --> 00:44:45,375
tell the world who it really is,

481
00:44:46,416 --> 00:44:50,208
or else the soul it possesses will die.

482
00:44:52,250 --> 00:44:54,208
So Phii Pong is like a thief, then?

483
00:45:01,000 --> 00:45:02,041
Okay, that'll do.

484
00:45:02,708 --> 00:45:03,625
Let's go, Sergeant.

485
00:45:04,666 --> 00:45:06,500
I'll be counting on you, Uncle.

486
00:45:06,583 --> 00:45:07,625
Hmm.

487
00:45:08,291 --> 00:45:09,375
Oh, wait.

488
00:45:13,791 --> 00:45:15,000
Here. Here.

489
00:45:15,833 --> 00:45:16,916
Mm.

490
00:45:18,291 --> 00:45:19,500
Take this.

491
00:45:20,083 --> 00:45:22,791
Keeps ghosts away. Keeps evil out.

492
00:45:24,541 --> 00:45:25,375
Thank you.

493
00:45:59,666 --> 00:46:02,166
SRI CHIANG KHAN STREET, SOI 19

494
00:46:03,333 --> 00:46:05,791
Three bags for 100 baht. They're suede.

495
00:46:12,750 --> 00:46:14,625
Two porridge and steamed rice. One bowl.

496
00:46:14,708 --> 00:46:15,583
Sure thing.

497
00:46:17,875 --> 00:46:19,375
You two should have a beer.

498
00:46:20,125 --> 00:46:21,041
I can drive you.

499
00:46:25,250 --> 00:46:26,500
Un, well…

500
00:46:27,291 --> 00:46:29,000
Are you sure
that's a good idea, Inspector?

501
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:31,708
Ask me again and I'll say "No."

502
00:46:31,791 --> 00:46:33,625
- Oh, hey, two beers, please.
- Coming.

503
00:46:57,208 --> 00:46:58,041
Here.

504
00:46:59,000 --> 00:47:01,541
That's all there is. That's all I've got.

505
00:47:11,000 --> 00:47:12,250
Is that all?

506
00:47:18,083 --> 00:47:19,125
Hello?

507
00:47:19,708 --> 00:47:20,625
Yes, I am.

508
00:47:21,541 --> 00:47:23,916
<i>Inspector, the DNA results just came in,</i>

509
00:47:25,666 --> 00:47:28,083
<i>and the DNA does not match Mr. Narong's.</i>

510
00:47:29,333 --> 00:47:31,875
<i>I've sent you some information</i>
<i>by email.</i>

511
00:47:31,958 --> 00:47:33,791
<i>Please take a look at it, Inspector.</i>

512
00:47:35,458 --> 00:47:37,875
<i>Cases like this have happened</i>
<i>in other provinces.</i>

513
00:47:38,500 --> 00:47:41,666
<i>And in every case,</i>
<i>teeth were missing from the bodies.</i>

514
00:47:54,416 --> 00:47:55,583
That plot of land,

515
00:47:56,416 --> 00:47:57,916
it's a waste for it to sit empty.

516
00:47:59,791 --> 00:48:00,791
Sign it over.

517
00:48:01,791 --> 00:48:04,291
You've taken enough. No way.

518
00:48:05,208 --> 00:48:06,125
That's all!

519
00:48:21,625 --> 00:48:23,291
<i>Back then, how do you remember it?</i>

520
00:48:24,583 --> 00:48:28,250
I remember people started hanging
those scarecrows.

521
00:48:29,958 --> 00:48:30,875
MUED

522
00:48:30,958 --> 00:48:34,416
It wasn't the cops.
It was the shaman around here

523
00:48:35,000 --> 00:48:36,958
<i>just repeating the same thing for years.</i>

524
00:48:37,625 --> 00:48:39,625
<i>How long have you been doing this, Uncle?</i>

525
